       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like it could be a typo.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and there is no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum for inflammatory conditions)\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO three times daily** (typical for pain or dysmenorrhea)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into doses such as 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a brief rationale. I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
